            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">$1,050 repatriation + $250 admin</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">$5,000 immigration + $5,000 treasury</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">$250 admin fee</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-white font-semibold">Physical Presence for Validity</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">1 visit every 2 years</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">1 visit every 2 years</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">Continuous stay authorized</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-white font-semibold">CRS Tax Certificate Feasibility</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-emerald-400 font-semibold">High (Requires 183d or center)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">Very High (Direct permanent)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-rose-400">Low (DGI rarely issues for temp)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- H2: Tax Residency Certificate & CRS Defense -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6 border-b border-slate-800 pb-3">
      3. The Golden Shield: Securing the DGI Tax Residency Certificate (Certificado de Residencia Fiscal)
    </h2>
    <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-4 mb-8">
      <p>
        Holding an immigration residency card (<em>carné de residente permanente</em>) does not automatically furnish you with bulletproof tax defense against aggressive western tax administrations. Under Common Reporting Standard (CRS) protocols, international banks will look through empty residential shell cards unless backed by a <strong>Certificado de Residencia Fiscal</strong> issued by the Dirección General de Ingresos (DGI).
      </p>
      <p>
        Governed by <strong>Executive Decree 958 of 2013</strong> and <strong>Law 33 of 2010</strong>, the DGI will grant a formal Tax Residency Certificate under two alternative statutory tests:
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4 my-4">
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl">
          <div class="text-emerald-400 font-bold text-sm mb-1 font-mono">Test 1: The 183-Day Physical Presence Standard</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Spending more than 183 days (consecutive or alternate) in the Republic of Panama during the fiscal year. Documented conclusively via passport entry/exit stamps verified by the National Immigration Service (Servicio Nacional de Migración).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl">
          <div class="text-cyan-400 font-bold text-sm mb-1 font-mono">Test 2: Center of Vital & Economic Interests</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Establishing your permanent home (via long-term lease or residential title in Panama City/Coronado), utility bills in your personal name, holding active bank accounts, and maintaining your principal commercial affairs anchored locally, even if physical presence is less than 183 days.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Armed with this certificate and an active Panamanian Tax ID (RUC - <em>Registro Único de Contribuyente</em>), you can submit self-certifications to international financial institutions (Interactive Brokers, Wise, Revolut, foreign banks), designating Panama as your primary and exclusive tax jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2: Banking Architecture & Corporate Structuring -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6 border-b border-slate-800 pb-3">
      4. Banking Architecture: Local Panamanian Banks vs International EMI Rails
    </h2>
    <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-4 mb-8">
      <p>
        Panama’s domestic banking sector—anchored in the International Banking Center with over 60 licensed private and foreign banks—is historically conservative. Compliance teams at institutions such as Banco General, Banistmo, and Global Bank operate under rigorous Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and FATF scrutiny.
      </p>
      <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 my-4">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 font-mono text-emerald-400">
          Optimal FinTech & Banking Stack for Remote Founders
        </h4>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
