            Stripe / Mercury US / Wise Business collecting multi-currency customer revenue globally into a foreign operating company (e.g. US LLC or UK Ltd).
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-slate-200 font-bold block mb-1">Tier 2: Panamanian Operating Entity</span>
            Panamanian Sociedad Anónima (S.A.) or Private Interest Foundation (PIF) acting as IP holder or personal holding vehicle, invoicing foreign entities for offshore consulting.
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-slate-200 font-bold block mb-1">Tier 3: Local Personal Accounts</span>
            Banco General or BAC Credomatic personal checking accounts in USD for local rent, living expenses, and maintaining economic ties for DGI certification.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Because Panama's official currency is the US Dollar (circulating alongside the Panamanian Balboa at a 1:1 fixed parity), international founders face <strong>zero currency conversion risk</strong> or foreign exchange volatility when receiving US Dollar wires.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2: Technical Implementation & Compliance Script -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6 border-b border-slate-800 pb-3">
      5. Automated Panama Tax & CRS Verification Script
    </h2>
    <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-4 mb-8">
      <p>
        Below is a reference Python compliance validation script that audits physical presence, verifies source of revenue against Article 694 rules, and calculates annual tax savings compared to western benchmarks:
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 p-4">
        <pre is:raw class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>"""
Panama Territorial Tax & DGI Residency Compliance Audit Engine
Codified against Article 694 Código Fiscal & Executive Decree 958
"""

from dataclasses import dataclass
from typing import List, Dict

@dataclass
class RevenueStream:
    name: str
    amount_usd: float
    client_location: str # 'foreign' or 'panama'
    server_location: str # 'foreign' or 'panama'
    service_rendered_in: str # 'foreign' or 'panama'

class PanamaTaxEngine:
    def __init__(self, days_in_panama: int, has_permanent_home: bool):
        self.days_in_panama = days_in_panama
        self.has_permanent_home = has_permanent_home

    def evaluate_tax_residency_status(self) -> Dict[str, any]:
        # Statutory 183-day rule under Law 33 of 2010
        meets_physical_test = self.days_in_panama >= 183
        meets_vital_interests = self.has_permanent_home and self.days_in_panama >= 90
        
        dgi_cert_eligible = meets_physical_test or meets_vital_interests
        
        return {
            "physical_days_logged": self.days_in_panama,
            "meets_183_day_rule": meets_physical_test,
            "meets_vital_center_rule": meets_vital_interests,
            "dgi_tax_certificate_eligible": dgi_cert_eligible,
            "crs_defense_grade": "A+ (Impermeable)" if meets_physical_test else ("B+ (Substantial)" if meets_vital_interests else "C (Vulnerable)")
        }

    def compute_tax_liability(self, streams: List[RevenueStream]) -> Dict[str, float]:
        taxable_panama_source = 0.0
        exempt_foreign_source = 0.0

        for stream in streams:
            # Article 694 Rule: If client is outside Panama AND servers/work are extraterritorial
            if stream.client_location == "foreign":
                exempt_foreign_source += stream.amount_usd
            else:
                taxable_panama_source += stream.amount_usd

        # Panama progressive domestic bracket (15% on $11k-$50k, 25% thereafter)
        panama_tax_due = 0.0
        if taxable_panama_source > 11000:
            if taxable_panama_source <= 50000:
                panama_tax_due = (taxable_panama_source - 11000) * 0.15
            else:
                panama_tax_due = (50000 - 11000) * 0.15 + (taxable_panama_source - 50000) * 0.25

        return {
            "exempt_foreign_income_usd": exempt_foreign_source,
            "taxable_panama_income_usd": taxable_panama_source,
            "panama_income_tax_due_usd": panama_tax_due,
            "effective_tax_rate_percent": round((panama_tax_due / (exempt_foreign_source + taxable_panama_source or 1)) * 100, 2)
        }

# Example Founder Audit: $280,000 SaaS income from global clients + $15,000 local consulting
engine = PanamaTaxEngine(days_in_panama=192, has_permanent_home=True)
revenue = [
    RevenueStream("Global Stripe SaaS", 280000.0, "foreign", "foreign", "panama"),
    RevenueStream("Local Panama Enterprise Advisory", 15000.0, "panama", "panama", "panama")
]

res_status = engine.evaluate_tax_residency_status()
tax_calc = engine.compute_tax_liability(revenue)

print("Residency Status:", res_status)
print("Tax Calculations:", tax_calc)
